  "effMFU": "How Much Computing Power Are We Actually Using?\n\nMFU compares the model's useful training computation per second with the hardware's theoretical peak computing power.\n\nM\nF\nU\n=\n𝐹\ns\nt\ne\np\n𝑡\ns\nt\ne\np\n×\n𝑁\nG\nP\nU\n×\n𝑃\np\ne\na\nk\n×\n100\n%\nMFU=\nt\nstep\n\t​\n\n×N\nGPU\n\t​\n\n×P\npeak\n\t​\n\nF\nstep\n\t​\n\n\t​\n\n×100%\nSYMBOL\tMEANING\tUNIT\n\n𝐹\ns\nt\ne\np\nF\nstep\n\t​\n\n\tUseful model FLOPs for one training step\tFLOPs\n\n𝑡\ns\nt\ne\np\nt\nstep\n\t​\n\n\tTraining step time\ts\n\n𝑁\nG\nP\nU\nN\nGPU\n\t​\n\n\tNumber of GPUs\tcount\n\n𝑃\np\ne\na\nk\nP\npeak\n\t​\n\n\tPeak compute per GPU\tFLOP/s\n\nM\nF\nU\nMFU\tModel FLOPs Utilization\t%\n\nIllustrative DeepSeek V4.1 Flash MFU — Not Measured. The training batch size (100.6M tokens/step) is reported in the technical report; FLOPs/token, GPU count, and step time are hypothetical teaching assumptions.\n\nTraining Step Time: 6.0 s\nTraining FLOPs per Token: 60 GFLOPs\nStep 1 — Useful model FLOPs per training step\n𝐹\ns\nt\ne\np\n\t\n=\n𝑁\nt\no\nk\ne\nn\ns\n×\n𝐹\nt\no\nk\ne\nn\n\n\n\t\n=\n100,600,000 tokens\n×\n60.00 GFLOPs\n\n\n\t\n=\n6.04 EFLOPs\nF\nstep\n\t​\n\n\t​\n\n=N\ntokens\n\t​\n\n×F\ntoken\n\t​\n\n=100,600,000 tokens×60.00 GFLOPs\n=\n6.04 EFLOPs\n\t​\n\n\t​\n\nStep 2 — Total hardware peak throughput\n𝑃\nt\no\nt\na\nl\n\t\n=\n𝑁\nG\nP\nU\n×\n𝑃\np\ne\na\nk\n\n\n\t\n=\n2\n,\n048\n×\n989.5 TFLOP/s\n\n\n\t\n=\n2,026,496 TFLOP/s\nP\ntotal\n\t​\n\n\t​\n\n=N\nGPU\n\t​\n\n×P\npeak\n\t​\n\n=2,048×989.5 TFLOP/s\n=\n2,026,496 TFLOP/s\n\t​\n\n\t​\n\nStep 3 — MFU\nM\nF\nU\n\t\n=\n𝐹\ns\nt\ne\np\n𝑡\ns\nt\ne\np\n×\n𝑁\nG\nP\nU\n×\n𝑃\np\ne\na\nk\n×\n100\n%\n\n\n\t\n=\n6.04 EFLOPs\n6.0 s\n×\n2\n,\n048\n×\n989.5 TFLOP/s\n×\n100\n%\n\n\n\t\n≈\n49.6%\nMFU\n\t​\n\n=\nt\nstep\n\t​\n\n×N\nGPU\n\t​\n\n×P\npeak\n\t​\n\nF\nstep\n\t​\n\n\t​\n\n×100%\n=\n6.0 s×2,048×989.5 TFLOP/s\n6.04 EFLOPs\n\t​\n\n×100%\n≈\n49.6%\n\t​\n\n\t​\n\n50%\nMFU\n100% = hardware's theoretical peak\n\nUnder these illustrative assumptions, useful model training computations achieve throughput equivalent to approximately 49.6% of the hardware's theoretical peak.\n\nShow Calculation\nAdvanced Settings"
}